  "text": "Planning Document: docs/dcps/INNERWEST/Marrickville/Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 34 Tempe Reserve.pdf\n\nClause 9.34.1 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): It is essential that development with the precinct considers the potential  impacts to biodiversity including native fauna (includ ing T hreatened S pecies and Endangered P opulations); native vegetation (including Endangered Ecological C ommunities); and habitat elements (including  their condition , structure, function, connectivity and disturbance)\n\nClause 9.34.2 - heritage (heritage): To protect and preserve the identified period buildings within the precinct and encourage their sympathetic alteration or restoration.\n\nClause 9.34.2 - heritage (heritage): To protect the identified  Heritage Items  within the precinct.\n\nClause 9.34.2 - height_limit (development_control): To maintain distinctly single storey streetscapes that exist within the precinct.\n\nClause 9.34.2 - heritage (heritage): To protect grou ps or runs of buildings which retain t heir original form including roof forms, original detailing and finishes.\n\nClause 9.34.2 - other (development_control): To protect  significant streetscape s and/or public domain elements within the precinct including landscaping, fencing, open space, sandstone kerb ing and guttering, views and vistas an d prevailing subdivision patterns.\n\nClause 9.34.2 - other (development_control): To support pedestrian and cyclist access, activity and amenity including maintaining and enhancing the public domain quality.\n\nClause 9.34.2 - zoning (land_use_zoning): To preserve the predominantly low density residential ch aracter of the precinct.\n\n",
